<title>PHILIPPINES: Jollibee sees 1996 net up 10-15 pct vs 1995.</title>
<headline>Jollibee sees 1996 net up 10-15 pct vs 1995.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine fast-food giant Jollibee Foods Corp said on Friday it expects to post a 10 to 15 percent growth in net income in 1996 from the year-ago 537.4 million pesos.</p>
<p>Jollibee's vice president for finance Raffy de la Rosa told Reuters that the company's new 1996 profit forecast is lower than an earlier 20 percent growth projection.</p>
<p>The firm is expected to register 20 percent growth this year compared to the 1996 figures, he said.</p>
</text>
